<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεύσ-της</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεύδω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>liar, cheat,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.261
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ ψ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.209
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Si.</u>
				15.8
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧν . . ψεῦσται
				φανούμεθα</span> wherein we shall be found to be <i>liars,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1195
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1127b16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.70
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1457.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Adj., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψευδής</span>
			, <i>lying, false,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					5.29
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεύστης δ᾽ οὗτος ἔπεστι
			λίθος,</span> of a cenotaph, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.273
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ψεύσταν δέ με τύμβον . .
				θέντο: τί θαῦμα; Κρῆτες ὅπου ψεῦσται, καὶ Διός ἐστι
				τάφος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				275
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Gaet.
			</span></i>), alluding to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρῆτες ἀεὶ ψεῦσται,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epimenid.
				1
			</span></i>, which is cited by <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Jov.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Tit.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>.</div>
